"""
FINAL ANALYSIS (S1-S4)
Question: In which century did "Diversity in Pottery Form" collapse and
"Diversity in Pottery Decoration" increase simultaneously?

Primary record : capital.csv -> ZKeform (pottery-FORM diversity, z),
                 Zkeverz (pottery-DECORATION diversity, z); fixed 100-year bin grid,
                 BCE labels treated as BIN LABELS (study convention).
Secondary      : time_series_data.csv PotteryForm_inter / PotteryDecoration_inter
                 (annual LINEAR interpolations of the same anchors; used ONLY for
                  smoothing / slope corroboration).
Context only   : Dagger / HouseSize / Sickle / Amber z-series, Belau+Woserin pollen
                 openness -- NOT used to date the step.

Pre-registered criteria, reported for every 100-year step:
 (a) direction : dFORM<0 AND dDEC>0 in the SAME step (simultaneity)
 (b) threshold : dFORM <= -2 SD(dFORM series) AND dDEC >= +2 SD(dDEC series)
 (c) divergence: composite = dDEC - dFORM, ranked + z-scored over all steps
 (d) smoothing : 100-y centred rolling mean of interpolated series, change over the
                 preceding 100 y at the step endpoint (+ 200-y window sensitivity)
 (e) level/rank: percentile ranks of post-step level, rank shift, state = record-low
                 form AND top-decile decoration
"""
import numpy as np, pandas as pd
pd.set_option("display.width", 240); pd.set_option("display.max_rows", 300)
OUT = "outputs"
pctr = lambda s: s.rank(pct=True)

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ S1 load/parse
bin_ = pd.read_csv("data/capital.csv")
for c in [c for c in bin_.columns if c.startswith("Z")]:
    bin_[c] = pd.to_numeric(bin_[c].astype(str).str.replace(",", "."), errors="coerce")
bin_["CE"] = -bin_["BCE"]
bin_ = bin_.sort_values("CE").reset_index(drop=True).rename(columns={"ZKeform": "FORM", "Zkeverz": "DEC"})
ann = pd.read_csv("data/time_series_data.csv", index_col=0)
F, D = "PotteryForm_inter", "PotteryDecoration_inter"

anch = ann.dropna(subset=["PotteryForm"])[["CE", "PotteryForm", "PotteryDecoration"]]
chk = anch.merge(bin_[["CE", "FORM", "DEC"]], on="CE", how="left")
ident = max((chk.PotteryForm - chk.FORM).abs().max(), (chk.PotteryDecoration - chk.DEC).abs().max())
reb = bin_.set_index("CE")[["FORM", "DEC"]].reindex(ann.CE.values).interpolate("linear", limit_area="inside")
ilin = max(np.nanmax(np.abs(ann[F].values - reb["FORM"].values)), np.nanmax(np.abs(ann[D].values - reb["DEC"].values)))
print("S1 bin grid : %d bins, BCE %d -> %d, step %s, missing %d" % (len(bin_), bin_.BCE.iloc[-1],
      bin_.BCE.iloc[0], np.unique(-np.diff(bin_.CE.values)), int(bin_[["FORM", "DEC"]].isna().sum().sum())))
print("S1 identity : max |annual raw anchor - capital bin value| = %.3f  (%d/%d anchors matched)"
      % (ident, chk.FORM.notna().sum(), len(chk)))
print("S1 interp   : max |*_inter - linear interp(bins)| = %.1e -> annual file adds no information" % ilin)

# ------------------------------------------- S2 criteria (a),(b),(c),(e) on bins
b = bin_[["CE", "BCE", "group", "FORM", "DEC"]].copy()
b["dFORM"] = b.FORM.diff(); b["dDEC"] = b.DEC.diff()
sdF, sdD = b.dFORM.std(), b.dDEC.std()
b["z_dFORM"] = b.dFORM / sdF; b["z_dDEC"] = b.dDEC / sdD
b["a_direction"] = (b.dFORM < 0) & (b.dDEC > 0)
b["b_collapse2sd"] = (b.dFORM <= -2 * sdF) & (b.dDEC >= 2 * sdD)
b["composite"] = b.dDEC - b.dFORM
b["z_composite"] = (b.composite - b.composite.mean()) / b.composite.std()
b["rank_composite"] = b.composite.rank(ascending=False, method="min")
b["pct_FORM_post"] = pctr(b.FORM); b["pct_FORM_prior"] = pctr(b.FORM).shift(1)
b["pct_DEC_post"] = pctr(b.DEC); b["pct_DEC_prior"] = pctr(b.DEC).shift(1)
b["rank_shift_FORM"] = b.pct_FORM_post - b.pct_FORM_prior
b["rank_shift_DEC"] = b.pct_DEC_post - b.pct_DEC_prior
b["e_state"] = (b.FORM <= b.FORM.min() + 1e-9) & (b.pct_DEC_post >= 0.75)  # top-quartile: 0.97 is a 7-way tie
# NOTE: with a 7-way tie at DEC=0.97 no percentile cut above 0.846 can include it, so the
# pre-registered "top decile" is implemented as top-quartile; (e) is CORROBORATIVE only -
# it is also satisfied by later bins of the same flat post-transition plateau.

# ------------------------------------------- S2 criterion (d): smoothing on annual
sm = ann.set_index("CE")[[F, D]].rolling(101, center=True, min_periods=51).mean()
ch1, ch2 = sm.diff(100), sm.diff(200)
for c in ["s100_FORM", "s100_DEC", "s100_FORM_rank", "s100_DEC_rank", "d_sign_agree", "s200_FORM", "s200_DEC"]:
    b[c] = pd.Series([None] * len(b), dtype="object")
for i in b.index:
    ce = int(b.CE[i])
    if ce in ch1.index:
        x1, x2 = ch1.loc[ce], ch2.loc[ce]
        b.loc[i, "s100_FORM"] = x1[F]; b.loc[i, "s100_DEC"] = x1[D]
        b.loc[i, "s100_FORM_rank"] = int((ch1[F] < x1[F]).sum()) + 1
        b.loc[i, "s100_DEC_rank"] = int((ch1[D] > x1[D]).sum()) + 1
        b.loc[i, "d_sign_agree"] = bool(x1[F] < 0 and x1[D] > 0)
        b.loc[i, "s200_FORM"] = x2[F]; b.loc[i, "s200_DEC"] = x2[D]
b["d_sign_agree"] = b.d_sign_agree.astype(object)
b["DECISIVE_a_b_c"] = b.a_direction & b.b_collapse2sd & (b.rank_composite == 1)
b["ALL_CRITERIA"] = b.DECISIVE_a_b_c & (b.d_sign_agree.astype(str) == "True") & b.e_state

cols = ["BCE", "group", "FORM", "DEC", "dFORM", "dDEC", "z_dFORM", "z_dDEC", "a_direction",
        "b_collapse2sd", "composite", "z_composite", "rank_composite", "pct_FORM_post",
        "rank_shift_FORM", "pct_DEC_post", "rank_shift_DEC", "e_state", "d_sign_agree",
        "DECISIVE_a_b_c", "ALL_CRITERIA"]
print("\nSD of century-to-century changes: dFORM %.3f, dDEC %.3f  -> 2-SD thresholds %.3f / %.3f"
      % (sdF, sdD, -2 * sdF, 2 * sdD))
print("\n===== RANKED CANDIDATE STEPS (top 8 by composite dDEC-dFORM) =====")
print(b.nlargest(8, "composite")[cols].round(3).to_string(index=False))
print("\n===== ALL STEPS SATISFYING (a) simultaneous opposite directions =====")
print(b[b.a_direction][cols].round(3).to_string(index=False))
ex = b[b.a_direction & ~b.b_collapse2sd]
print("\n===== (a)-steps REJECTED by the 2-SD collapse threshold (b): %d found =====" % len(ex))
if len(ex): print(ex[cols].round(3).to_string(index=False))
print("\n===== RUNNER-UP KEPT VISIBLE: step ending 1000 BCE bin vs selected step =====")
print(b[(b.CE == -1000) | (b.CE == -1700)][cols + ["s100_FORM", "s100_DEC", "s100_FORM_rank",
      "s100_DEC_rank", "s200_FORM", "s200_DEC"]].round(3).to_string(index=False))
print("\n===== CRITERION TALLY (all %d steps) =====" % int(b.dFORM.notna().sum()))
print(pd.Series({"steps_total": int(b.dFORM.notna().sum()), "pass_a_direction": int(b.a_direction.sum()),
                 "pass_b_2SD_directional": int(b.b_collapse2sd.sum()),
                 "pass_c_composite_rank1": int((b.rank_composite == 1).sum()),
                 "pass_d_smooth_sign": int((b.d_sign_agree == 1).sum()),
                 "pass_e_state": int(b.e_state.sum()), "pass_DECISIVE_a_b_c": int(b.DECISIVE_a_b_c.sum()),
                 "pass_ALL_incl_d_e": int(b.ALL_CRITERIA.sum())}).to_string())
print("\nsteps whose 100-y smoothed endpoint change is form-down & dec-up (criterion d sign test):",
      list(b.loc[b.d_sign_agree.astype(str)=="True","BCE"]))
print("NOTE: (d) as a pure SIGN test is not discriminative (many years have opposite-signed 100-y changes);"
      "\n      the dating claim is carried by (a)+(b)+(c) magnitude criteria, with (d)/(e) as corroboration.")

# ------------------------- CONTROL: form floor without a decoration rise (EN bins)
print("\n===== CONTROL: every bin at the record-low FORM value (z = -1.13) =====")
ctrl = b[b.FORM <= b.FORM.min() + 1e-9][["BCE", "group", "FORM", "DEC", "pct_DEC_post", "dFORM", "dDEC", "a_direction"]]
print(ctrl.round(3).to_string(index=False))
full = b[b.FORM <= b.FORM.min() + 1e-9]
en, post = full[full.group == "EN"], full[full.CE <= -1700]
print("EN floor bins %s have decoration at the record LOW (%.2f) -> same-direction move, NOT simultaneous."
      % (list(en.BCE), en.DEC.iloc[0]))
print("Post-transition floor bins (%d bins, %dBCE->%dBCE) have decoration %.2f-%.2f; the floor is only read as a"
      " COLLAPSE for the single step where decoration rises simultaneously (bin %dBCE)."
      % (len(post), int(post.BCE.iloc[-1]), int(post.BCE.iloc[0]), post.DEC.min(), post.DEC.max(), int(post.BCE.iloc[-1])))
print("Correlation of bin-level FORM vs DEC over all %d bins: %.3f (strong inverse coupling)" % (len(b), b.FORM.corr(b.DEC)))
print("Largest downward form rank-shift among all steps: %.3f ; largest upward decoration rank-shift: %.3f"
      % (b.rank_shift_FORM.min(), b.rank_shift_DEC.max()))

# --------------------------------------------- CONTEXT ONLY (never used for dating)
ctx = ann.set_index("CE"); lo, hi = -1800, -1700
rows = []
for s in ["Dagger_inter", "HouseSize_inter", "Sickle_inter", "Amber_inter", "CopperGold_inter",
          "Depot_inter", "MonumentCount_inter", "HatchetSword_inter", "AxesCelts_inter", "MonumentSize_inter"]:
    chg = ctx.loc[hi, s] - ctx.loc[lo, s]
    rows.append((s, round(ctx.loc[lo, s], 2), round(ctx.loc[hi, s], 2), round(chg, 2), round(chg / ctx[s].diff(100).std(), 2)))
print("\n===== CONTEXT ONLY: co-varying capital indicators across the 1800 -> 1700 BCE step =====")
print(pd.DataFrame(rows, columns=["series", "z@1800BCE", "z@1700BCE", "change", "z_vs_100y_SD"]).to_string(index=False))
pol = pd.read_csv("data/pollen_openness_score_Belau_Woserin_Feeser_et_al_2019.csv")
for c in pol.columns[1:]:
    pol[c] = pd.to_numeric(pol[c].astype(str).str.replace(",", "."), errors="coerce")
o = pol.dropna(subset=["SMOOTH_MEAN_100y"]).set_index("CE").SMOOTH_MEAN_100y
print("CONTEXT ONLY: Belau+Woserin openness (SMOOTH_MEAN_100y): %.2f @1900BCE, %.2f @1800BCE, %.2f @1700BCE, "
      "%.2f @1600BCE, %.2f @1500BCE (whole-record mean %.2f)"
      % (o.loc[-1900], o.loc[-1800], o.loc[-1700], o.loc[-1600], o.loc[-1500], o.mean()))
print("CONTEXT ONLY: period labels of the bins involved: "
      + ", ".join("%dBCE=%s" % (r.BCE, r.group) for r in b[(b.CE >= -2000) & (b.CE <= -1400)].itertuples()))

# ------------------------------------------------------------ ASCII figure (no mpl)
v = b[(b.CE >= -2500) & (b.CE <= -500)].reset_index(drop=True)
W = 5
print("\nASCII chart 2500-500 BCE:  | = PotteryForm z (ZKeform)   # = PotteryDecoration z (Zkeverz)   X = both")
for lvl in np.arange(1.8, -2.05, -0.4):
    row = ""
    for r in v.itertuples():
        ch = " "
        if abs(r.FORM - lvl) <= 0.2: ch = "|"
        if abs(r.DEC - lvl) <= 0.2: ch = "X" if ch == "|" else "#"
        row += ch.ljust(W)
    print("%+5.1f |%s" % (lvl, row))
print("       +" + "-" * (W * len(v)))
print("        " + "".join(str(r.BCE).ljust(W) for r in v.itertuples()) + "   (bin label, BCE)")
print("        " + "".join(("^step" if r.BCE == 1700 else " " * W) for r in v.itertuples()) + "   <- end bin of the selected 100-year step")

# --------------------------------------------------------------- ROBUSTNESS checks
madF = 1.4826 * b.dFORM.abs().median(); madD = 1.4826 * b.dDEC.abs().median()
rob_tbl = []
for lab, (aF, aD) in {"SD 2.0": (2 * sdF, 2 * sdD), "SD 1.5": (1.5 * sdF, 1.5 * sdD),
                      "SD 2.5": (2.5 * sdF, 2.5 * sdD), "robust MAD 2.0": (2 * madF, 2 * madD)}.items():
    ok = b[(b.dFORM <= -aF) & (b.dDEC >= aD)]
    rob_tbl.append((lab, round(aF, 3), round(aD, 3), len(ok), ",".join(str(int(x)) for x in ok.BCE)))
print("\n===== ROBUSTNESS of the 2-SD directional threshold =====")
print(pd.DataFrame(rob_tbl, columns=["threshold rule", "|form| cut", "|dec| cut", "n steps passing", "bin(s)"]).to_string(index=False))
print("Robust MAD-scaled SDs: form %.3f, decoration %.3f" % (madF, madD))
for w in [100, 200, 250]:
    sw = ann.set_index("CE")[[F, D]].rolling(w + 1, center=True, min_periods=max(31, w // 2)).mean().diff(w).dropna()
    print("smooth %3dy window: most negative form change at %d BCE (%.2f) & most positive decoration change at %d BCE (%.2f)"
          % (w, sw[F].idxmin(), sw[F].min(), sw[D].idxmax(), sw[D].max()))
print("=> wider smoothing windows move the extreme a few decades later, i.e. the data identify an INTERVAL, not a year.")

# ------------------------------------------------------------ outputs / final answer
b.to_csv(f"{OUT}/pottery_bins_candidate_steps.csv", index=False)
ann[["CE", "calBP", F, D]].to_csv(f"{OUT}/pottery_interpolated_annual.csv", index=False)
sel = b[b.ALL_CRITERIA]
print("\n===== FINAL SELECTED STEP =====")
print(sel[cols + ["s100_FORM", "s100_DEC", "s100_FORM_rank", "s100_DEC_rank", "s200_FORM", "s200_DEC"]].round(3).to_string(index=False))
sel.to_csv(f"{OUT}/selected_step.csv", index=False)
assert len(sel) == 1
g = lambda col, ce: b.loc[b.CE == ce, col].iat[0]
HYP = f"""HYPOTHESIS / ANSWER

Diversity in Pottery Form (ZKeform, capital.csv; numerically identical to PotteryForm/PotteryForm_inter,
time_series_data.csv) and Diversity in Pottery Decoration (Zkeverz == PotteryDecoration/PotteryDecoration_inter)
diverge simultaneously in exactly ONE 100-year step of the fixed 100-year grid: the step from the 1800 BCE bin to
the 1700 BCE bin, c. 1800-1700 BCE. Form falls {g('FORM',-1800):+.2f} -> {g('FORM',-1700):+.2f} z
(delta {g('dFORM',-1700):+.2f}, {g('z_dFORM',-1700):+.2f} SD of its own century-to-century changes, the record
decline) while decoration rises {g('DEC',-1800):+.2f} -> {g('DEC',-1700):+.2f} z (delta {g('dDEC',-1700):+.2f},
{g('z_dDEC',-1700):+.2f} SD, its record rise); the divergence index delta_DEC - delta_FORM =
{g('composite',-1700):.2f} (z {g('z_composite',-1700):+.2f}) is {g('composite',-1700)/b.nlargest(2,'composite').composite.iloc[1]:.1f}x
the runner-up. Simultaneity criterion: form decline AND decoration rise inside the SAME 100-year step, the decline
qualifying as a collapse against that variable's own century-to-century variability (2-SD directional test; unique
also at 1.5 SD, 2.5 SD and MAD-robust scalings). Of {int(b.dFORM.notna().sum())} steps, only this one has the two
constructs moving in opposite directions at all.

CENTURY: headline = the 18th century BCE (the change step spans 1800-1700 BCE; 1800-1701 BCE is the 18th century
BCE under strict ordinal counting). The collapse/increase is recorded in the 1700 BCE bin, and the new state - form
pinned at its record low {b.FORM.min():+.2f}, decoration {g('DEC',-1700):+.2f} - occupies the 1700-1100 BCE bins,
decoration rising further to +1.53 in the 1000 BCE bin. Under loose "1700s BCE" usage, or naming the first full bin
in the new state (1700-1601 BCE), the same event is the 17th century BCE / "c. 1700 BCE"; both phrasings describe
this identical transition step.

CONTROL (why simultaneity matters): form also reaches its record-low value in the Early Neolithic bins
4300-4100 BCE, but there decoration is at its record LOW (-1.92) - concordant, not divergent. The runner-up step,
ending in the 1000 BCE bin, raises decoration (+0.56) while form is FLAT at its floor (delta 0.00): diversification
inside an already-collapsed form system, not a simultaneous collapse+increase. Both are excluded.

CONTEXT ONLY (no dating weight): LN->OBA boundary immediately after the step (1800/1700 BCE = LN, 1600 BCE = OBA);
Dagger -3.74 (z -5.3), HouseSize -1.57, Sickle -1.01 decline in the same step while Depot/CopperGold/MonumentCount
are unchanged; Belau+Woserin openness (SMOOTH_MEAN_100y) falls 2.34 (1800 BCE) -> 1.53 (1600 BCE) against a
record mean of -0.21. We therefore hypothesise that the reorganisation of pottery tradition at the Late Neolithic /
Early Bronze Age transition - fewer vessel FORMS but a broader decorative repertoire - belongs to a wider
reconfiguration of material and social capital at declining land-clearance intensity.

LIMITATIONS: (1) timing within c. 1800-1700 BCE is unidentifiable (one value per 100-year bin; the annual series is
a linear interpolation, verified to {ilin:.0e}); (2) the standardisation base of the z-values is unknown, so
"collapse" is relative to the series' own century-to-century variability (SD {sdF:.3f} form, {sdD:.3f} decoration),
and treating ZKeform/Zkeverz as standardised DIVERSITY proxies is a metadata-borne assumption, not a finding;
(3) later bins repeat identical values (form {b.FORM.min():+.2f} for 1700-500 BCE; decoration +0.97 for seven bins,
then +1.53 for six), indicating period-averaged rather than genuinely centennial sampling, so "century" is a
resolution limit of the source data.
"""
with open(f"{OUT}/answer_statement.txt", "w") as f:
    f.write(HYP)
print("\n----- FINAL ANSWER (outputs/answer_statement.txt) -----\n" + HYP)
print("\nwrote outputs/pottery_bins_candidate_steps.csv, outputs/pottery_interpolated_annual.csv,"
      " outputs/selected_step.csv, outputs/answer_statement.txt")
